 and its protection. The spec describes the heater output as going only through U6 to J6.\", \"expected\": \"The heater control GPIO should drive only the TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN pins, D2 and R3. The spec documents the heater output as going only through U6 to J6, with no direct external connection to the GPIO net.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"J5\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"Pin_2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"13\\\") (pinfunction \\\"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Drives a single **heater output** net through a smart high-side switch (`U6`, TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1) switched from the ESP32's GPIO1\"}], \"impact\": \"An external load or short on J5 would connect directly to the MCU GPIO, with no current limit or fault reporting from the high-side switch. The GPIO could be damaged, and the terminal could be driven without the switch's protection.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}]}",
